386→                        <div id="content">Is it true that if $A\subseteq\mathbb{N}$ is such that\[\frac{1}{\log\log x}\sum_{n\in A\cap [1,x)}\frac{1}{n}\to \infty\]then\[\left(\sum_{n\in A\cap [1,x)}\frac{1}{n}\right)^{-2} \sum_{\substack{a,b\in A\cap (1,x]\\ a&#60;b}}\frac{1}{\mathrm{lcm}(a,b)}\to \infty?\]</div>
